    "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 20-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2 / HfO2 / SiO2. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Optimize a 20-layer dielectric stack on fused silica substrate under air incidence. Material sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2 (20 finite layers total). Initialize layer thicknesses from the round 3 optimum candidate (thicknesses_nm: [35.09, 47.65, 35.10, 47.62, 35.10, 47.59, 35.06, 47.53, 34.97, 47.56, 34.95, 47.56, 35.07, 47.62, 35.07, 47.65, 35.08, 47.62, 35.07, 42.69]) but apply random perturbation of ±6 nm to layers 6 through 14 only (indices 5-13 in zero-based counting). Hold layers 1-5 and 15-20 at their round 3 optimum values during initialization. Perform bounded gradient-based thickness optimization with per-layer bounds of ±15 nm from initialized values. Spectral objectives: maximize mean transmittance 255-280 nm, minimize mean transmittance 300-700 nm, minimize mean transmittance 700-1100 nm. Normal incidence, unpolarized light. No metal layers. Fused silica substrate. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 255–280 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Transmittance in 300–700 nm; Transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers; No metal layers; Only conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials.",
